From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sqz kernel recipe <sqz-kernel@squeezefs>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] io_uring/kbuf: finish a short bulk allocation with reclaiming
 pages

io_region_allocate_pages_multi_buf() (kernel-managed buffer rings, patch
0003) backs each buffer with one compound allocation of
get_order(buf_size) and, when that fails, with alloc_pages_bulk_node(),
treating any short count as -ENOMEM.

The bulk allocator is not a reclaiming allocator.  It batches order-0
pages from the per-cpu lists of a zone that sits above its low
watermark plus the request, and when no zone qualifies it falls back to
the regular allocator for a single page; with memcg kmem accounting
online - the default as soon as any memory cgroup exists - a
__GFP_ACCOUNT request skips the batch and returns that one page.  So a
buffer whose compound allocation fails, which for a costly order (a
1 MiB buffer is order 8 with 4 KiB pages) is routine once the page
cache has filled and fragmented memory, comes back short, and the whole
registration fails with -ENOMEM while gigabytes of clean page cache
could be reclaimed.  On a 62 GiB x86_64 host whose 54 GiB page cache
was churned by buffered 4 KiB random reads (MemFree 345-472 MiB while
registering, a few MiB of it in free order >= 8 blocks of ZONE_NORMAL),
registering the 32 x 1 MiB kmbuf ring of a FUSE-over-io_uring queue
failed with -ENOMEM in 10 of 10 attempts, each after five retries over
1.2 s.

Finish a short buffer page by page with alloc_page() and the same gfp,
which may enter direct reclaim, as vm_area_alloc_pages() does when the
bulk allocator comes back short for vmalloc.  Fail with -ENOMEM only if
a single page cannot be had, or once the task has a fatal signal
pending (no reclaiming on behalf of a task that is going away).  The
failure path is unchanged and releases every page allocated so far.
---
 io_uring/memmap.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/io_uring/memmap.c b/io_uring/memmap.c
index 0fa0475f8..0bdb87f52 100644
--- a/io_uring/memmap.c
+++ b/io_uring/memmap.c
@@ -205,6 +205,22 @@ static int io_region_allocate_pages_multi_buf(struct io_mapped_region *mr,
 
 		nr_allocated = alloc_pages_bulk_node(gfp, NUMA_NO_NODE,
 						     buf_pages, cur_pages);
+		/*
+		 * The bulk allocator draws on the free lists above the low
+		 * watermark and reclaims for at most one page (it returns a
+		 * single page under memcg kmem accounting): finish the buffer
+		 * with the reclaiming single-page allocator.
+		 */
+		while (nr_allocated < buf_pages) {
+			struct page *page;
+
+			if (fatal_signal_pending(current))
+				break;
+			page = alloc_page(gfp);
+			if (!page)
+				break;
+			cur_pages[nr_allocated++] = page;
+		}
 		if (nr_allocated != buf_pages) {
 			unsigned int total =
 				(cur_pages - pages) + nr_allocated;
